<https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/SpecificationType/specification> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A specification is a detailed document (or set of documents) that describes the requirements, design, behavior, or other characteristics of a system, component, or process so that all stakeholders have a clear, unambiguous reference."@en .
<https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/supportLevel> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "supportLevel provides an indication of what support expectations that the\nsupplier of an artifact is providing to the user."@en .
<https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/RelationshipType/hasTest> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Every to Element is a test artifact for the from Element (from hasTest to), during a LifecycleScopeType period."@en .
